#: fec319631b1448fbb6f788ef38d14439
msgid "Foundations"
msgstr "理论基础"

#: 8641783c413b4bf3b2cb731d42f3fcab
msgid ""
"Diátaxis is successful because it *works* - both users and creators have a "
"better experience of documentation as a result. It makes sense and it feels "
"right."
msgstr "Diátaxis 之所以成功，是因为它*有效*——用户和创建者都因此获得了更好的文档体验"
"。它说得通，感觉也对。"

#: 59f54ad2c37e410fad2fd673b679eb57
msgid ""
"However, that's not enough to be confident in Diátaxis as a theory of "
"documentation. As a theory, it needs to show *why* it works. It needs to "
"show that there is actually some reason why there are exactly four kinds of "
"documentation, not three or five. It needs to demonstrate rigorous thinking "
"and analysis, and that it stands on a sound theoretical foundation."
msgstr "然而，这还不足以让我们放心地把 Diátaxis 当作一套文档理论。作为理论，它必须说"
"明自己*为什么*有效。必须说明文档恰好是四类、而非三类或五类，背后确有缘由。还"
"必须展示严谨的思考与分析，证明自己立足于坚实的理论基础。"

#: d125ba031fa448ceb331fddbf89df8f9
msgid ""
"Otherwise, it will be just another useful heuristic approach, and the "
"strongest claim we can make for it is that \"it seems to work quite well\"."
msgstr "否则，它不过是又一种有用的启发式方法，而我们能为它作出的最强论断，也不过是“"
"它似乎还挺管用”。"

#: cd124bc7ae834854b4897cdde46ca7cc
msgid "Two dimensions of craft"
msgstr "技艺的两个维度：知与行、学与用"

#: bca7be6623524ca8b334b13452b2886a
msgid ""
"Diátaxis is based on the principle that documentation must serve the needs "
"of its users. Knowing how to do that means understanding what the needs of "
"users are."
msgstr "Diátaxis 基于这样一条原则：文档必须服务于其用户的需求。要知道如何做到这一点"
"，就要弄清用户的需求是什么。"

#: 5943642b0d374e4ca996676a2f11877c
msgid ""
"The user whose needs Diátaxis serves is *the practitioner in a domain of "
"skill*. A domain of skill is defined by a craft - the use of a tool or "
"product is a craft. So is an entire discipline or profession. Using a "
"programming language is a craft, as is flying a particular aircraft, or even"
" being a pilot in general."
msgstr "Diátaxis 所服务的用户，是*某一技能领域的实践者*。技能领域由一门技艺界定——使"
"用一件工具或产品是技艺，一整个学科或职业也是。使用一门编程语言是技艺，驾驶某"
"一型飞机是技艺，甚至泛泛地当一名飞行员，也是技艺。"

#: 8d2ea77c498e4b1dbc078ba995bfb363
msgid ""
"Understanding the needs of these users means in turn understanding the "
"essential characteristics of craft or skill."
msgstr "理解这些用户的需求，也就意味着要理解技艺或技能的本质特征。"

#: 3d6d516307ed41b7a316d2f0af19b09e
msgid "Action/cognition"
msgstr "知与行"

#: 68769a428e464bb4809b30eda3fc4acb
msgid ""
"A skill or craft or practice contains both **action** (practical knowledge, "
"knowing *how*, what we do) and **cognition** (theoretical knowledge, knowing"
" *that*, what we think). The two are completely bound up with each other, "
"but they are counterparts, wholly distinct from each other, two different "
"aspects of the same thing."
msgstr "一门技能、一种技艺或一项实践，都同时包含**行（行动）**（实践知识、知道*怎么"
"做*、我们所做的事）和**知（认知）**（理论知识、知道*是怎么回事*、我们所想的"
"）。二者完全交织在一起，却又互为对应，彼此截然不同，是同一件事的两个不同方面"
"。"

#: c8a92a8d27c5478f9cb459b6caffda8a
msgid "Acquisition/application"
msgstr "学与用"

#: 1f9c2c27b2b942cb902a25193c7a949e
msgid ""
"Similarly, the relationship of a practitioner with their practice is that it"
" is something that needs to be both **acquired**, and **applied**. Being "
"\"at work\" (concerned with applying the skill and knowledge of their craft)"
" and being \"at study\" (concerned with acquiring them) are once again "
"counterparts, distinct but bound up with each other."
msgstr "同样，实践者与自己的实践之间也有双重关系：既需要**习得（学）**，也需要**应用"
"（用）**。“处于工作状态”（关注的是应用自己技艺的技能和知识）与“处于学习状态”"
"（关注的是习得它们）同样互为对应，既彼此区分，又相互交织。"

#: d432d672fc544981b20618fdbba74838
msgid "The map of the territory"
msgstr "领域地图"

#: 15cd97147fa04a0683dccec4bbbb7b55
msgid ""
"This gives us two dimensions of skill, that we can lay out on a map - a map "
"of the territory of craft:"
msgstr "这样，我们便得到技能的两个维度，可以把它们铺陈在一张地图上——一张技艺领域的地"
"图："

#: f43870fbbb02402f92f28847f98fcf62 915328085b384934886dd134246db9dd
msgid "The territory of craft as a two-dimensional map"
msgstr "以二维地图呈现的技艺领域"

#: 28c0a32f86b0423aba373426d377c08e
msgid ""
"This is a *complete* map. There are only two dimensions, and they don't just"
" cover the entire territory, they define it. This is why there are "
"necessarily four quarters to it, and there could not be three, or five. It "
"is not an arbitrary number."
msgstr "这是一张*完整的*地图。维度只有两个，而这两个维度不仅覆盖整个领域，还界定了这"
"个领域。因此它必然有四个象限，不可能是三个，也不可能是五个。这个数字不是随意"
"定下的。"

#: a09cf34de127447eb0880e64bbe82c0b
msgid ""
"It also shows us the *qualities* of craft that define each of them. When the"
" idea that documentation must serve the needs of craft is applied to this "
"map, it reveals in turn what documentation must be and do to fulfil those "
"obligations - in four distinct ways."
msgstr "它还让我们看到界定每一个象限的技艺*品质*。把“文档必须服务于技艺的需求”这一理"
"念放到这张地图上，就会进而揭示出：为履行这些义务，文档必须成为什么、必须做什"
"么——而且是四种截然不同的方式。"

#: 7007146631cd437c8ac6eb3772d80592
msgid "Serving needs"
msgstr "服务需求"

#: e1b8bb920ac24255abacbf10edcbd1eb
msgid ""
"The map of the territory of craft is what gives us the familiar Diátaxis map"
" of documentation. The map is in effect an answer to the question: what must"
" documentation do to align with these qualities of skill, and to what need "
"is it oriented in each case?"
msgstr "技艺领域的地图，正是我们熟悉的 Diátaxis 文档地图的来源。实际上，这张地图回答"
"的是这样一个问题：文档必须做什么，才能与这些技能的品质相契合；而在每一种情形"
"下，它面向的又是哪一种需求？"

#: 1a09e0d1c53542d0bd78ae770cb29099
msgid ""
"We can see how the map of documentation addresses *needs* across those two "
"dimensions, each need also defined by the characteristics of its quarter of "
"the map."
msgstr "我们可以看到，文档地图如何在那两个维度上回应*需求*；而每一种需求，也由它所在"
"象限的特征来界定。"

#: 2d973d487969406bb7a24151966620f5
msgid "need"
msgstr "需求"

#: 2fef7cc884bc419bbe03ff8741ad65dc
msgid "addressed in"
msgstr "由……回应"

#: a21c07300bbb4a6298f1088bfd637791
msgid "the user"
msgstr "用户"

#: 20726ba0e98049a28e75d5869c262902
msgid "the documentation"
msgstr "文档"

#: b96955993e28498b839fc5849744abeb
msgid "learning"
msgstr "学习"

#: f8b763a56b3746d58756dc2e840dbea6
msgid "tutorials"
msgstr "教程"

#: 71bed2e58cb546c9ad1564dd3eb9524a 7408849212de4a67896114cb09bed1b6
msgid "acquires their craft"
msgstr "习得（学）技艺"

#: a745f7c2ae384920a61b86424f319f7c 9cb5e5b161bb4bf1a98b94eed440880f
msgid "informs action"
msgstr "指导行动（行）"

#: 05325e08276a447ca87f77126635f79c
msgid "goals"
msgstr "目标"

#: a5670f3c861b414eae84fcc69201df55
msgid "how-to guides"
msgstr "实践指南"

#: a7a1aacf466649f28710d2a468d9e961 fc2c056760a243b59f41dbbf18df1301
msgid "applies their craft"
msgstr "应用（用）技艺"

#: 7ae66dac5c8f41cf977aebc34e351167
msgid "information"
msgstr "信息"

#: 16f5c558a40745189540a1b0f41057f1
msgid "reference"
msgstr "参考资料"

#: 5a27ba57d48a49a381a2895880d24de3 eed2283995a84877a34aa5a4f59df884
msgid "informs cognition"
msgstr "帮助认知（知）"

#: 42c3ec02df6740b88483ee663c0e727f
msgid "understanding"
msgstr "理解"

#: 2055e3bbff7e4efcbe004e86d44254df
msgid "explanation"
msgstr "解释说明"

#: 673c4efeb51d4e8c95cfc4a5bcbfafab
msgid ""
"The Diátaxis map of documentation is a memorable and approachable idea. But,"
" a map is only reliable if it adequately describes a reality. Diátaxis is "
"underpinned by a systematic description and analysis of generalised **user "
"needs**."
msgstr "Diátaxis 文档地图是一个好记、易懂的概念。但地图唯有充分描述现实，才算可靠。"
"Diátaxis 的根基，是对一般化**用户需求**的系统描述与分析。"

#: 136fdadb841348599cc9192f58ff1d66
msgid ""
"This is why the tutorials, how-to guides, reference and explanation of "
"Diátaxis are a complete enumeration of the types of documentation that serve"
" practitioners in a craft. This is why there are four and only four types of"
" documentation. There is simply no other territory to cover."
msgstr "正因如此，Diátaxis 的教程、实践指南、参考资料和解释说明，才完整地列举了为某"
"种技艺的实践者服务的文档类型。正因如此，文档有且仅有四类。除此之外，根本没有"
"别的领域需要覆盖。"
